Looking at the test failures, the issue is in the `flowLow=FALSE` branch: when the condition disappears with `alarmAcked=TRUE` already set, the alarm isn't being cleared. According to S6, alarmActive should clear when condition is gone AND alarm was already acknowledged (no new ack edge needed).

Let me trace through a3→a4:
- a3: flowLow=TRUE, alarmAcked becomes TRUE via rising edge
- a4: flowLow=FALSE, but my code only clears on `risingAck`, which is FALSE → alarm stays active

The fix: check if condition just disappeared (`prev_flowLow=TRUE`) to distinguish "condition just went away" from "condition still gone from before".

```st
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB
VAR_INPUT
    flowLow   : BOOL;
    ackBtn    : BOOL;
    sensorOK  : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    alarmActive : BOOL;
    alarmAcked  : BOOL;
    highHigh    : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
    prev_flowLow : BOOL := FALSE;
    prev_ackBtn  : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR

VAR_TEMP
    risingAck : BOOL;
END_VAR

risingAck := ackBtn AND NOT prev_ackBtn;

IF flowLow THEN
    // Condition is active
    IF NOT alarmActive THEN
        // New alarm activation
        alarmActive := TRUE;
        alarmAcked  := FALSE;
    ELSIF risingAck THEN
        // Rising ack while condition still exists - just mark acknowledged
        alarmAcked := TRUE;
    END_IF;
ELSE
    // Condition has disappeared
    IF prev_flowLow AND alarmAcked THEN
        // Condition just cleared, was already acknowledged - clear immediately
        alarmActive := FALSE;
        alarmAcked  := FALSE;
    ELSIF prev_flowLow AND NOT alarmAcked THEN
        // Condition just cleared, unacknowledged - enter pending clear state
        alarmAcked := TRUE;
    ELSIF risingAck AND alarmAcked THEN
        // Condition still gone from before, pending clear - clear on new ack
        alarmActive := FALSE;
        alarmAcked  := FALSE;
    END_IF;
END_IF;

// High priority alarm: sensor failure (independent)
highHigh := NOT sensorOK;

// Update state for next cycle
prev_flowLow := flowLow;
prev_ackBtn  := ackBtn;

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
```

